What is okdl?
-------------
okdl is a command-line tool for downloading videos from OK.ru. It is a wrapper around yt-dlp that automatically normalizes OK.ru URLs and applies a runtime fix for a known JSON parsing bug in the OK.ru extractor.

Installation
------------
1. sudo apt update
2. sudo apt install -y curl ffmpeg python3 python3-venv
3. python3 -m venv .venv
4. source .venv/bin/activate
5. pip install --upgrade pip
6. pip install yt-dlp
7. curl -O https://raw.githubusercontent.com/agb-777/okdl/main/okdl.py
8. chmod +x okdl.py

Usage
-----
python3 okdl.py -u <URL> [OPTIONS]

Basic Examples
--------------
- List available formats:
  python3 okdl.py -u "https://ok.ru/video/91456710947561" -F
- Download best quality:
  python3 okdl.py -u "https://ok.ru/video/91456710947561"
- Download a specific format by ID:
  python3 okdl.py -u "https://ok.ru/video/91456710947561" -f hls-3014
- Download with a custom filename:
  python3 okdl.py -u "https://ok.ru/video/91456710947561" -o "my_video.%(ext)s"
- Enable verbose output:
  python3 okdl.py -u "https://ok.ru/video/91456710947561" -v

